# Day 68 Assignment – Transformer vs LSTM Comparison

## Objective

Compare a Transformer Encoder and an LSTM model on the same IMDB sentiment classification dataset.

## Dataset

IMDB Movie Reviews Dataset.

## Models Implemented

1. Transformer Encoder
2. LSTM Classifier

## Transformer Components

- Token Embeddings
- Sinusoidal Positional Encoding
- Multi-Head Self-Attention
- Residual Connections
- Layer Normalization
- Feed-Forward Network
- Global Average Pooling
- Dense Classification Layer

## Experimental Setup

Both models use the same training and testing dataset, vocabulary size, maximum sequence length, batch size, number of epochs and optimizer.

## Evaluation Metrics

- Test Accuracy
- Test Loss
- Training Time
- Training and Validation Accuracy

## Observations

The Transformer Encoder processes sequence positions in parallel through self-attention, whereas the LSTM processes the sequence recurrently.

The actual accuracy and training time are recorded in `outputs/model_comparison.csv`.

## Conclusion

This experiment demonstrates the architectural differences between Transformer Encoders and LSTMs. It also provides a practical comparison of their classification performance and computational time on the same dataset.
